Package: introcompfinr
Title: Functions used in Introduction to Computational Finance and Financial Econometrics With R
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Eric", "Zivot", , "ezivot@uw.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: This package accompanies the book Introduction to Computational Finance 
    and Financial Econometrics with R. The package contains all of the data for the 
    book example as well as functions to estimate simple models for asset returns,
    implement mean-variance portfolio theory with and without short-sales constraints,
    and perform asset and portfolio risk analytics.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports: 
    corrplot,
    matrixStats,
    quadprog,
    xts,
    zoo
Suggests:
    PerformanceAnalytics
Depends: 
    R (>= 3.5)
LazyData: true
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
